Living creatures do not rely on just one sense. A monster guards its territory using both sight and hearing simultaneously!

### Multi-Sensor Fusion:
When you combine multiple sensors, your robot can make sophisticated, multi-factor decisions using C++ boolean logic:

#### 1. Logical AND (`&&`) — Both Conditions Required:
Suppose we want a **Night-Watch Sentry**: the alarm should only wake up if it is pitch dark in the room **AND** someone sneaks within 20 cm of the guard post!

```cpp
if (lightLevel < 250 && distanceCm < 20) {
  digitalWrite(alarmLed, HIGH); // Intruder lurking in the shadows!
} else {
  digitalWrite(alarmLed, LOW);
}
```

#### 2. Logical OR (`||`) — Either Condition Triggers:
Suppose we want an **Emergency Security Alarm**: trigger if an object is dangerously close **OR** if an intruder turns on a flashlight:

```cpp
if (distanceCm < 10 || lightLevel > 800) {
  digitalWrite(alarmLed, HIGH); // Emergency breach!
}
```

### Prioritized Conditions:
What if sensor readings conflict? By ordering `if`, `else if`, and `else` blocks strategically, you establish clear priority hierarchy so safety rules always take precedence over everyday tasks!
